r and backend, writing the database queries that make that fast, implementing smart logic on this data and building integrations for the growing number of third-party consumers of our services.</p><br><strong>Your challenge</strong><p><strong>Key responsibilities</strong><ul><li>Build and extend features end-to-end that handle large volumes of geospatial data, with attention to UX and design</li><li>Architect and build services that integrate large amounts of heterogenous data to enable users to prioritize a vast number of competing tasks</li><li>Own the next major evolution of our public API </li><li>Drive the continuous development of our agentic solutions</li><li>Lead cross-functional teams, driving new feature developments from very early in a topic, through discovery, design, architecture to release and maintenance. Take real ownership </li></ul><strong>How we work</strong><br>Our development lifecycle is a pragmatic scrumban: structured enough to coordinate, loose enough to move fast. Engineers here have real autonomy - you will make plenty of decisions yourself, and you will have senior engineers to think out loud with on the ones that carry more weight. Asking is normal here, at every level.<br>We take agentic development seriously but we are, sometimes painfully, aware of its limits. Tickets with solid acceptance criteria become agentic specs that agents implement in test-driven setups. Code review is a mix of agent and human - whichever is most effective for the change at hand. We ship to production at least weekly. And we actively encourage engineers to keep coding and debugging manually to stay sharp; the goal is augmented engineers, not engineers who've forgotten how to program.<br><br><strong>Stack</strong><ul><li>Frontend: React, Typescript</li><li>Backend: NestJS, Prism, Typescript</li><li>Database: PostgreSQL (including geospatial workloads)</li><li>Infrastructure &amp; CI/CD: Gitlab</li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p><strong>Must have</strong><ul><li>Expert backend experience with ideally NestJS, Express, or Node.js</li><li>A very good understanding of cloud architecture</li><li>Solid TypeScript and React in production (Vue, Preact or Angular also fine — we care that you know a component model well, not which one)</li><li>You've used AI-assisted coding in your actual day-to-day, not just tried it once</li></ul><strong>Nice to have</strong><ul><li>Spec-driven or test-driven development, agentic or otherwise</li><li>Python - even better if you were previously exposed to many other different programming paradigms</li><li>Web-based geospatial / GIS work</li><li>An eye for design and UX — enough to make small design calls without needing a mockup for everything</li></ul>You do not need all of the "nice to haves," and you do not need to match every "must have" perfectly. If you read this and think you'd be a good fit but you're missing a line item, apply and tell us what you'd bring instead.</p><br><strong>Your Benefits</strong><p><ul style="border:0px solid;font-family:Inter, '-apple-system', 'system-ui', 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', 'Open Sans', 'system-ui', '-apple-system', 'Segoe UI', Roboto, Ubuntu, Cantarell, 'Noto Sans', sans-serif, 'Apple Color Emoji', 'Segoe UI Emoji';font-size:14px;font-style:normal;font-weight:400;text-transform:none;"><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">The opportunity to create a product that can improve business processes and lives across the globe.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">Flexible working hours and hybrid work model - we trust our employees to get their work done while maintaining a healthy work-life balance.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">We empower employees to drive their own career development, take initiative and have the freedom to be creative and bold.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">Not an overtime culture - we take care that overtime is done only as a necessity and always offset with time off and rest.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">A collaborative and learning environment - frequent internal workshops, knowledge sharing sessions, journal clubs and hackathons.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">Office located in the centre of Berlin Kreuzberg with free fruit, nuts and drinks.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">Potential to participate in the employee stock option program.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">Urban Sports membership and BVG subsidy, corporate pension program.</li><li style="border:0px solid;margin:0px;">A diverse and vibrant international environment of 30+ different nationalities.</li></ul></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/liveeo-gmbh/senior-full-stack-engineer-liveeo-gmbh-berlin-office-hybrid-304401","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"LiveEO GmbH Berlin Office (Hybrid)","created_at":1791144572},{"slug":"senior-full-stack-engineer-liveeo-gmbh-berlin-office-hybrid-239663","company_name":"LiveEO GmbH","title":"Senior Full Stack Engineer (f/m/x)","description":"<br><strong>Build the Market Leader in Satellite Analytics with us at LiveEO</strong><p>We are looking for a Senior Full Stack Engineer to help shape the next stage of SurfaceScout, one of LiveEO's core products. SurfaceScout turns satellite data into reliable, actionable insights for the operators of critical infrastructure. You'll take ownership of significant parts of the SurfaceScout application, from the user-facing experience to the services and data flows behind it, and help evolve it into an even more scalable and reliable product. This is a high-ownership role on an established, fast-growing product: part hands-on engineering, part systems design, part technical leadership within the squad. You'll work across the full product lifecycle, from shaping and building new features, to strengthening the architecture and engineering practices that support long-term growth, using a modern TypeScript and Python stack.</p><br><strong>Your challenge</strong><p>As a Senior Full Stack Engineer on the SurfaceScout squad, you'll take ownership of significant parts of a live, growing product, turning ideas into reliable production systems and strengthening the architecture that supports long-term growth.<br><br><strong>Core responsibilities include:</strong><br><ul><li>Design and build features end to end (TypeScript &amp; Python), translating product requirements into reliable, well-tested systems that ship to customers.</li><li>Define and implement integrations with LiveEO's platform and data services, ensuring clean interfaces, reliable data flows, and extensibility for future development.</li><li>Collaborate across teams to reuse and adapt shared components, aligning on architecture, APIs, and engineering standards across products.</li><li>Own key architectural decisions (service boundaries, data models, deployment patterns), balancing speed of delivery with long-term maintainability and reliability.</li><li>Iterate quickly on feedback from product, customers, and stakeholders, evolving features into robust, production-grade solutions.</li><li>Raise the bar for the squad: mentor teammates, review code, and help shape technical direction as a senior voice on the team.</li><li>Champion engineering best practices (code quality, documentation, testing, observability), keeping the codebase healthy as the product scales.</li><li>Contribute across the stack, from backend services and APIs to frontend interfaces, delivering a cohesive and usable end-to-end experience.</li></ul></p><br><strong>Your profile</strong><p><ul><li>Strong engineering fundamentals in TypeScript and Python, with a focus on writing clean, maintainable, and well-structured code.</li><li>Several years building and shipping full stack applications in production, including backend services, APIs, and m