&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;It is Yext’s policy to provide reasonable accommodations to people with disabilities as required by applicable law. If you have a disability that requires an accommodation in completing this application, interviewing, or participating in the employee selection process, please complete&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSexIHU2ZCgSpcOcz5DHaL9Eyk0GIqz-AqdbgbdV8ImC74qkWA/viewform?usp=sf_link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; data-saferedirecturl=&quot;https://www.google.com/url?q=https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSexIHU2ZCgSpcOcz5DHaL9Eyk0GIqz-AqdbgbdV8ImC74qkWA/viewform?usp%3Dsf_link&amp;amp;source=gmail&amp;amp;ust=1630682825064000&amp;amp;usg=AFQjCNEM4K7q8h4cF_oXrXEx8WRpI8YsLA&quot;&gt;this form&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Security Alert&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;All legitimate Yext communications come from ----- email addresses. Messages from other domains (for example, ----- are not authorized and are likely fraudulent. If you receive a message that seems suspicious, do not share personal information, click on links, or provide payment. Instead, please report the communication to&amp;nbsp;&lt;a ----------<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/yext/senior-customer-success-manager-london-173112","tags":["(8) Enterprise CS"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1791161703},{"slug":"account-manager-uk-london-81963","company_name":"Fonio","title":"Account Manager (UK)","description":"<h1><strong>About fonio</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We grew from $1M to $10M ARR in under 12 months and now serve 10,000+ customers.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fonio is Europe’s market leader for AI phone agents for SMBs. Now we’re expanding globally and into new products.<br />We move fast, take ownership, give direct feedback, and avoid politics and unnecessary meetings.<br />Join one of <strong>Europe’s fastest-growing companies</strong>.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Your Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">You actively manage our existing customer accounts and act as their primary point of contact across the entire customer lifecycle. Your focus is on continuously increasing the value our AI phone assistant delivers, expanding use cases, and identifying additional potential.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You regularly run review, discovery, and upsell conversations with existing customers, analyse their usage, and demonstrate how our AI can automate further processes and deliver measurable impact.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You own expansion revenue within your customer portfolio — from upgrades and add-ons to renewals — working towards clear monthly and quarterly quotas.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Alongside the commercial side, you carry a strong customer success component: you ensure customers are successfully onboarded, use the product optimally, and stay satisfied long-term. You bring market feedback back into the team in a structured way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work closely with Customer Success, Product, and Marketing, ensuring clean handovers, reliable forecasts, and a well-maintained pipeline in the CRM.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What to Expect</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Account Ownership:</strong> Responsibility for your own existing-customer portfolio with a clear focus on upsell &amp; retention.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Expansion Sales:</strong> Identifying and realising growth potential within existing accounts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Success Focus:</strong> Regular touchpoints, QBRs, and proactive support to maximise customer success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pipeline &amp; Forecast:</strong> Structured account planning, clean CRM maintenance, and reliable revenue forecasting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Teamwork:</strong> Close collaboration with Customer Success, Product, and Marketing.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Impact:</strong> Actively shaping our account &amp; expansion motion in a fast-scaling AI startup.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">€65,000 – €95,000 OTE (base + uncapped commission, depending on experience)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">On-site in Vienna</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Top equipment of your choice &amp; extremely short decision-making paths</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Close collaboration with Product, Marketing &amp; Customer Success</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong, scaling AI product with real customer value</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 1 year of experience in B2B SaaS sales, account management, or customer success (startup/scale-up a plus)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in upselling, renewals, or expansion revenue across existing customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong product and technology understanding; you're highly AI-savvy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Structured working style, ownership mindset, and customer focus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Native-level English, confident in calls, reviews &amp; demos</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application Process</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">15 min recruiter intro call</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">45 min content interview incl. a short case study</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">20 min conversation on culture, expectations &amp; details</p></li></ol><hr><p>Compensation: £65K – £95K</p><ul><li>65-95k • Salary Range £65K – £95K</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fonio/account-manager-uk-london-81963","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1791160806},{"slug":"technical-success-analyst-uk-london-107559","company_name":"Marqeta Inc","title":"Technical Success Analyst - UK","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Marqeta is looking for a <strong>Technical Success Analyst</strong> to join our operations team and play a critical role in delivering Marqeta’s cutting-edge card issuing and payments platform to new customers. You’ll lead the technical onboarding of standardized products, support customers through implementation, and become a trusted voice both internally and externally. This role blends product expertise, customer advocacy, and a collaborative mindset to drive long-term client success and improve our implementation practices. If you’re motivated by building strong customer relationships, solving technical problems, and contributing to team growth, this could be the role for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>PLEASE NOTE: </strong>This is a hybrid role and requires employees to be based within 35 miles of our London office. You will be expected to work on-site two days a week, on Tuesday and Thursday, with the flexibility to work remotely on the other days.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Talent team will share more details if selected for the "Recruiter" Interview. We'd love for you to join us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Impact You'll Have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Lead Implementations</strong>: Own the configuration and deployment of Marqeta’s standardised products and services for new customers, interfacing with everyone from full stack engineers to founders/CEOs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Customer Support</strong>: Serve as the technical expert guiding customers through their integration journey, especially with our APIs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build Product Expertise</strong>: Develop deep knowledge of specific Marqeta products and services; create customer slide presentations,  internal runbooks and training content to scale team knowledge.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Advocate for Customers</strong>: Provide feedback to internal teams that reflects the customer’s voice and ensures our product evolves to meet real-world needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborate Cross-Functionally</strong>: Partner with Marqeta’s Project Managers, Product Managers, Sales, and Account Management to align and execute on client goals.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who You Are</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years of experience in a technical customer-facing role (e.g., solutions engineering, technical onboarding, or technical support).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional communication skills - you can explain complex technical concepts to anyone orally and in writing. Your friends and family consider you their go-to person for understanding new technologies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to manage projects independently and take initiative in solving problems.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Expert proficiency in REST APIs, Secure File Transfer Protocols (SFTP), SQL, and Datadog</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working across teams and building relationships with both clients and internal stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A customer-first mindset; skilled at understanding customer needs and designing practical solutions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strategic thinker who can connect daily work to broader business goals and team priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commitment to learning and contributing to the growth of others on the team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated strong understanding of fintech (e.g. acquiring, networks, point-of-sale) and card payments background, especially on the issuing side.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to prioritise, manage, and deliver on multiple projects simultaneously; highly motivated and able to work unsupervised against aggressive schedules.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice-To-Haves</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor's degree 