&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/gitlab/remote-major-account-executive-uk-public-sector-185493","tags":["EMEA - Enterprise"],"job_types":[],"location":"Remote","created_at":1791140104},{"slug":"remote-global-sales-director-of-smb-new-business-267208","company_name":"gitlab","title":"Global Sales Director of SMB, New Business","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;c-message_actions__container c-message__actions&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of New Business owns GitLab&#39;s end-to-end new-logo acquisition strategy — from pipeline generation through regional execution — and leads the org through four manager-level leaders: a New Business EMEA Manager, a New Business AMER Manager, a New Business BDR Manager, and a New Business SDR Manager. This is a new, expanded scope in our GTM organization, critical to building GitLab&#39;s customer base and continued long-term growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to sales leadership, you will be responsible for hiring, developing, and leading a team of managers — and, through them, their teams of BDRs, SDRs, and New Logo Account Executives — to meet and exceed new-business goals across regions. The right candidate is passionate about open source software, DevSecOps, and selling to development teams, with a proven track record leading multiple sales or pipeline-generation teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;c-message_actions__container c-message__actions&quot;&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Owns the end-to-end new-logo strategy across EMEA, AMER, and the BDR/SDR pipeline-generation functions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Leads, develops, and holds accountable four manager-level direct reports and, through them, their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds and iterates the outbound and top-of-funnel playbook spanning pipeline generation through regional deal execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sets a unified quota, territory, and coverage strategy across EMEA and AMER new-logo teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Builds cross-functional relationships and influences roadmaps across regions to drive new logos&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partners with senior sales, marketing, and RevOps leadership to align new-business strategy with corporate revenue goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drives cross-regional forecasting, pipeline health, and revenue reporting for the global new-business function&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyzes market dynamics across regions to maximize existing successes and create new growth opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Educates the org on industry factors: competitive products, regulations, trends, customer needs, and pricing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establishes and reports on team- and org-level metrics; addresses performance gaps across managers and their teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensures the new-business plan is aligned with and supports the corporate revenue goal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recruits and hires manager-level talent; invests time weekly building a pipeline of future manager and leadership hires&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fosters a successful, positive culture across a multi-region, multi-function org&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record leading multiple sales or pipeline-generation teams, ideally across regions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;History of exceeding new-business quotas at a team and org level, and coaching managers to do the same&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of B2B software sales experience, including 4+ years in a people-management role; experience managing managers (a &quot;manager of managers&quot;) strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success building and scaling outbound/top-of-funnel motions (BDR/SDR) alongside direct new-logo sales execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating across regions (EMEA and AMER ideally, APJ is a big bonus) with an understanding of regional market dynamics&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated resilience, intelligence, and creativity in building business cases and go-to-market strategy at an org level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to coach managers on team leadership, technical sales, and value-based selling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience selling to small &amp;amp; medium businesses; willingness to &quot;roll up your sleeves&quot; when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience utilizing CRM and marketing automation systems (Salesforce, Clari, Marketo, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong executive presence; ability to represent the new-business function to senior leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong relationship-building and negotiation skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation skills; executive-level written and verbal communication, with the ability to mentor managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You share our values, and work in accordance with those values&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/structure/#management-group&quot;&gt;Leadership at GitLab&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use GitLab&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel if needed and comply with the company&#39;s travel policy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: xx-small;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: white;&quot;&gt;Remote-Global&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The base salary range for this role’s listed level is currently for residents of the&amp;nbsp;United States only. This range is intended to reflect the role&#39;s base salary rate in locations throughout the US.&amp;nbsp;Grade level and salary ranges are determined through interviews and a review of education, experience, knowledge, skills, abilities of the applicant, equity with other team members, alignment with market data,&amp;nbsp;and geographic location.&amp;nbsp;The base salary range does not include any bonuses, equity, or benefits. See more information on our &lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLBeneUS&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;benefits&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#000000;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:none;font-family:&#39;Arial&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt; and &lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;waffle-rich-text-link&quot; href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/stock-options/&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-link=&quot;https://bit.ly/GLequity&quot; data-sheets-formula-bar-text-style=&quot;font-size:12px;color:#1155cc;font-weight:normal;text-decoration:underline;font-family:&#39;&#39;Arial&#39;&#39;;font-style:normal;text-decoration-skip-ink:none;&quot;&gt;equity&lt;/a&gt;. Sales roles are also eligible for incentive pay targeted at up to 100% of the offered base salary.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;United States Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$148,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$248,400 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/gitlab/remote-global-sales-director-of-smb-new-business-267208","tags":["Direct Sales - Global Digital"],"job_types":[],"location":"Remote","created_at":1791140104},{"slug":"operations-engineer-london-36081","company_name":"Odin","title":"Operations Engineer","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Odin is building the investment infrastructure for the future of private markets.<br />We believe capital is one of the most powerful tools for shaping the world - and more people should know how to put it to work. Our mission is to make it radically easier to raise and deploy capital, so that anyone, anywhere, can back the companies and ideas they believe in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first product is a full-stack platform for launching and running private investment firms, allowing you to run everything from your phone - think Shopify for VC and PE. We handle all the infrastructure: from legal structuring and investor onboarding to KYC/AML, payments, tax, reporting, and exits.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're already trusted by over 10,000 angels, VCs, and founders. We administer over $750m in assets, covering investments from pre-seed to series E. This includes household names like ElevenLabs, OpenAI, SpaceX, xAI, Anduril, etc. but also new companies creating everything from synthetic brains to small nuclear reactors.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why we're hiring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We are automating a decades old part of the financial services industry. AI pilled operators like you are the beating heart of this plan, because LLMs &amp; agents allow us to turn this services business entirely into software.</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're post-PMF, fast-growing, and rolling out new products (fund admin) &amp; geographies (USA). Customer &amp; deal volume is climbing fast.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today we're on track for roughly 700 deals a year, with a team of ~20, and we’ll process $500m-$750m of investment in 2026 alone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The next goal is 7,000 deals a year and billions in annual investment flows.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe this can be achieved with a team of around 50 people. But it will only be possible if we turn human-driven services workflows into software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The operational machine behind Odin is still held together in many places by people and spreadsheets. Your job is to come in, understand every process and system, simplify, streamline and automate the shit out of it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll be part of a small elite team embedded in operations and working closely with existing team members to build agents that automate work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We expect the right hire to be spending more time in Claude Code than in Excel, email or anything else.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Understand the work, then rebuild it:</strong> You’ll get close to how our operational teams actually work - the processes, edge cases, manual steps and things that slow them down. Your job is to understand them well enough to redesign, automate and build better ways of doing them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build and automate:</strong> You’ll turn manual workflows into tools, automations and systems that make the business faster and more scalable. You’ll work autonomously and move quickly - often vibe coding something useful yourself before it ever needs traditional product or engineering resource.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bridge operations and engineering:</strong> You’ll know when something can be solved with process, automation or a lightweight build, and when it genuinely needs deeper engineering work. When it does, you’ll bring Product, Design and Engineering in with the problem already understood, simplified and proven.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Delete things and say no:</strong> You’ll constantly question why a process exists, whether a request should be supported, and whether something is worth scaling. If a workflow exists for no good reason, you kill it. If a request creates complexity without enough value, we don’t do it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we're looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI-pilled builder: </strong>Clear evidence, at work or in your own time, that you've built concrete solutions to problems with no budget and no engineers. No-code tooling, scripts, spreadsheets, vibe-coded apps and more.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Numerate: </strong>Comfortable with financial mechanics, strong mental arithmetic. You’ll be working on automating a lot of numerical matters - carry, allocations, fee calculations, distributions, and the edge cases that make all of them interesting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In the details and extremely on top of things: </strong>You understand every single aspect of our systems end to end. You close loops, you chase, you push hard to get things done.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>First principles thinker: </strong>Although you're in the details and on top of execution, you also zoom out. You look at any process the way a good product manager looks at a product: What's the job? Why are we doing this at all? What's the smallest, simplest system that achieves the goal?<br />A lot of what happens in fund admin is inherited convention, an industry "given", or a constraint of some third party. You should find it physically difficult to accept any of that.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Big plus: regulated financial services background: </strong>Fund administration, custody, payments, brokerage, audit, tax or another back office function. Useful, but not required. SQL, serious Excel and other experience piping data between systems are all worth having too. However, we care much more about the traits you have and things you can build than specific skills or experience on your CV. If you're a few years into your career and you've already automated the shit out of your last job or built something incredible with AI, we want to talk to you.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You want to operate, not manage: </strong>Odin is not a place for middle management. We all get shit done, regardless of title or seniority</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There are five things we care about deeply:</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Reason from the ground up: </strong>Seek to understand what is true by always asking why. Do not trust convention or experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Speed begets speed: </strong>We work fast. Speed compounds, it's the best form of defensibility, and it's energising to be around. If you work slowly, or tolerate slow work around you, you do not belong at Odin.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Take ownership: </strong>Do not wait for permission to do things. Find the answer, force the thing into existence and hold others to an extremely high standard - the same standard you hold yourself to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Brutal honesty: </strong>If work doesn't meet the bar, people need to hear it, and the right people want to.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Truly excellent customer service: </strong>Be a stickler for detail in every single interaction a customer has with us, and always strive to make this experience better, smoother, faster.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role is probably not for you if</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather build product than operate. Product instinct is required in this role, but a product management career is not what this is;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You prefer close management of your responsibilities;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are risk-averse;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want a 9-5;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You take yourself too seriously;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You care about working for a company that’s raised lots of money rather than one that's extremely capital efficient and focused on building a profitable giant that has a positive economic impact</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">£70k - £90k base, plus a meaningful equity grant. We're flexible on the mix of cash and equity.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hiring process</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Three stages, usually inside two weeks, with detailed feedback within 24 hours of each one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location &amp; ways of working</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a London-based team. This role works closely with the founders, product and the wider ops team, and the speed we run at makes that much easier in-person. At least three days a week in the office.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health:</strong> Private health insurance (Vitality), paid sick leave including support for pregnancy loss and fertility treatments, and access to Spill for mental health support</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Wellness:</strong> £1,000 annual budget for health, therapy or fitness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Parental Leave:</strong> Enhanced maternity, adoption, paternity and partner leave</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pension:</strong> 4% employer contribution with salary sacrifice options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Time Off:</strong> 25 days annual leave, 2 wellness days and flexible bank holidays (33 days total)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Work From Anywhere:</strong> Up to 6 weeks per year working from anywhere globally</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Birthday Leave:</strong> An additional day of leave</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/odin/operations-engineer-london-36081","tags":["Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1791139202},{"slug":"senior-people-specialist-right-to-work-immigration-operations-hatfield-229420","company_name":"ocadogroup","title":"Senior People Specialist - Right to Work & Immigration Operations","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are Ocado Group, and we&#39;re bringing world-class automation to online grocery. Our Ocado Smart Platform (OSP) combines cutting-edge robotics, AI, and IoT within our advanced CFCs (Customer Fulfilment Centres). We&#39;ve mastered the single pick, transforming online delivery for our global partners. Join us and be part of a team pushing the boundaries of retail technology.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Location: UK-based&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Location &amp;amp; Attendance Requirements:&lt;br&gt;This is a UK-based role, which is fundamental to the position as it involves performing regular in-person Right to Work checks. Candidates must be based in the UK and available to attend the office on Monday mornings when required.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking either two part-time team members or 1 full time member to ensure full operational coverage across the working week. Both postholders will need to be available to attend the office on Monday mornings for in-person checks when required, with individual working schedules agreed upon to ensure seamless week-long support.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role drives UK Right to Work and immigration compliance for activities requiring in-country oversight. Working in close partnership with the Bulgaria Shared Services Centre which handles core case preparation and administration, the UK Specialist owns local employer checks, compliance activities, and Sponsorship Management System (SMS) administration. Ultimately, the role supports Ocado in meeting its sponsor licence and Right to Work obligations and delivers an efficient, high-quality experience for candidates and internal teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Right to Work Compliance&lt;br&gt;Execute RTW Checks: Perform online, video, and manual Right to Work checks, verifying Share Codes and identity documentation.&lt;br&gt;Complex Case Management: Resolve document/Experian exceptions, handle Employer Checking Service (ECS) requests, and support time-sensitive Day 1 / visa expiry cases.&lt;br&gt;Manual Check Review: Audit manager-led checks and partner with People Partners on escalations where evidence is incomplete.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Immigration &amp;amp; Sponsorship&lt;br&gt;CoS Administration: Create, assign, amend, and withdraw Defined and Undefined Certificates of Sponsorship (CoS) via the Sponsorship Management System (SMS).&lt;br&gt;Sponsor Licence Reporting: Manage mandatory Home Office reporting for job, salary, location, or status changes, as well as delays and terminations within statutory timelines.&lt;br&gt;Licence &amp;amp; Allocation Management: Monitor CoS allocation limits, execute SMS key user updates, and support the processing of sponsorship extensions and changes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Payments &amp;amp; Governance&lt;br&gt;Sponsorship Finance: Process UK-controlled CoS payments via Worldpay/PAID and maintain audit-ready financial records.&lt;br&gt;SSC Collaboration: Receive prepped case packs from the Bulgaria SSC, execute UK-specific compliance, and deliver seamless handoffs for downstream processing.&lt;br&gt;Continuous Improvement: Maintain compliance records, support internal/external audits, and continuously refine joint UK-Bulgaria operational workflows.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About You&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Previous experience of UK Right to Work processes.&lt;br&gt;Knowledge of Skilled Worker sponsorship and Certificates of Sponsorship.&lt;br&gt;Strong attention to detail and ability to work accurately with compliance-sensitive processes.&lt;br&gt;Comfortable following detailed procedures and working to fixed deadlines.&lt;br&gt;Confident handling personal and confidential employee information.&lt;br&gt;Strong organisation and case-management skills.&lt;br&gt;Ability to identify when a case falls outside the standard process and needs escalation.&lt;br&gt;Good written and verbal communication skills.&lt;br&gt;Comfortable working across multiple systems and maintaining accurate records.&lt;br&gt;Ability to work independently while working closely with a remote Shared Services team.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We Offer&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;We believe in supporting our people with meaningful, flexible benefits that prioritise well-being and work-life balance. Here’s a snapshot of what you can expect:&lt;br&gt;Time to recharge: 25 days annual leave (rising to 27 after 5 years), plus the option to buy more – and 30 days a year to work from anywhere in the world.&lt;br&gt;Health &amp;amp; wellbeing: Private Medical Insurance from your first month, wellbeing support through specialist apps and EAP, plus Income Protection and Life Assurance.&lt;br&gt;Family-first policies: 22 weeks paid maternity/primary carer leave and 6 weeks paid paternity leave.&lt;br&gt;Financial support: Pension with employer matching up to 7%, share schemes (Sharesave &amp;amp; BAYE), and interest-free loans for train tickets.&lt;br&gt;Commuter perks: Cycle to Work Scheme and free shuttle buses to/from Hatfield and Welwyn Garden City stations.&lt;br&gt;Exclusive discounts: 15% off at Ocado.com with free delivery (starting in your first month).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
