ht:1.3800000000000001;text-align:justify;margin-top:0pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"><span style="font-size:11pt;font-family:Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:transparent;font-weight:400;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;">WeCreate möchte einen inklusiven, diversen und authentischen Arbeitsplatz schaffen. Vielleicht bist genau du die Person, die diese Rolle weiterdenkt. Wir freuen uns, dich kennenzulernen.</span></p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/wecreate-germany/senior-social-brand-manager-all-genders-hybrid-282227","tags":["Social Media","Social Brand Manager","TikTok","Instagram","YouTube","Agentur"],"job_types":["Experienced","Temporary","Full time"],"location":"Hybrid","created_at":1791097791},{"slug":"senior-project-manager-hybrid-223640","company_name":"Arethia","title":"Senior Project Manager (m/f/d)","description":"<br><strong>Role description</strong><p>As Senior Project Manager, you will join our central Project Management team in Reinbek, which leads the company's large and complex cross-functional projects and sets the standards for how projects are run across all of arethia's global locations. Join us during a pivotal growth phase and help create the foundations of a team that will drive meaningful transformation across the organisation.<br><span style="font-size:14px;"><br></span><span style="font-size:14px;">You will independently lead complex projects with senior stakeholders across departments, and you will be the person we turn to when a project has drifted off course and needs to be brought back on track. </span><br><span style="font-size:14px;"><br></span><span style="font-size:14px;">This is a delivery role first, and it is also a chance to shape how project management works in a growing, international company: you will contribute to our standards and methods, support colleagues who run their own projects and help build a project management community across our sites. As the team grows, so does the scope of what you can take on.</span></p><br><strong>Your Mission</strong><p><ul><li>Project Leadership – Lead large, cross-functional projects independently from initiation to closure, including planning, governance, steering committees and stakeholder management.</li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Problem Solving - Facilitate and actively participate in problem-solving sessions to drive project success </span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Project Recovery – Take over projects that have drifted off course or lost their lead, diagnose what went wrong and re-establish structure as interim or permanent lead.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Stakeholder Management – Navigate demanding situations with senior leadership and across departments and prepare well-founded decisions for steering committees.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Quality and Coaching – Support department-led projects as quality assurance and sparring partner and coach project managers on their deliverables.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Standards and Methods – Contribute to our project management standards, templates and training formats, and turn project experience into reusable methods.</span></li></ul></p><br><strong>Minimum Qualifications</strong><p><ul><li>Bachelor's degree or equivalent practical experience.</li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Several years of experience independently leading complex, cross-functional projects with full ownership from initiation to closure.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Experience working with senior stakeholders and navigating conflicting interests across departments.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Strong analytical and problem solving skills.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Experience taking over or stabilising projects already in progress.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Ability to work independently, propose solutions and make decisions within your remit.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Business-level communication skills in German and English (C1).</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Experience in applying common project management tools, e.g. for task and milestone tracking.</span></li></ul></p><br><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong><p><ul><li>Experience with an ERP or comparable large-scale system implementation.</li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">IPMA Level C or equivalent. A higher level is a plus.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Experience in a manufacturing or regulated production environment.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Experience developing project management standards, templates or training formats.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Experience with Jira and Confluence.</span></li><li><span style="font-size:14px;">Experience working in an international, multi-site organisation.</span></li></ul></p><br><strong>Why you'll love working here</strong><p><ul><li>Exciting tasks in an internationally operating, growing family business with flat hierarchies</li><li>Flexible working hours and a hybrid working model</li><li>4 weeks remote work from other EU countries</li><li>30 days paid vacation per year</li><li>Salary bands for a fair corporate culture</li><li>Monthly allowance of €50 for your BAV</li><li>Annual 360° feedback loops with clear promotion criteria and an individual career path</li><li>Responsibility from day one in a company that encourages personal responsibility and growth</li><li>Relocation costs can be reimbursed on a pro rata basis</li><li>Regular company events such as summer party, Christmas party</li><li>Paid team dinners or activities for each team twice a year</li><li>Free parking right outside the door</li><li>Perks and benefits: JobRad, subsidized lunch, subsidy for the Deutschlandticket, free language courses and discounted memberships at several gyms and for the Wellpass</li><li>Fresh fruit, free drinks and snacks in the office</li></ul><br> </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/arethia/senior-project-manager-hybrid-223640","tags":[],"job_types":["Experienced","Permanent","Full time"],"location":"Hybrid","created_at":1791097756},{"slug":"senior-account-executive-france-france-office-paris-341352","company_name":"Lobster Data Gmbh","title":"(Senior) Account Executive - France","description":"<br><strong>Position Overview:</strong><p><p style="margin:0px 0px 13.3333px;padding:0px;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;background-color:transparent;text-align:left;"><span style="margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:13px;font-style:italic;line-height:18.6px;font-family:'Times New Roman', 'Times New Roman_EmbeddedFont', 'Times New Roman_MSCustomFont', 'Times New Roman_MSFontService', serif;"><span style="margin:0px;padding:0px;">This is a vacancy for a hybrid role based at our coworking office in Paris (9th arrondissement, Opéra). We encourage applications from all qualified candidates, regardless of gender identity. You will be on-site in Paris 2 days per week for close collaboration and alignment; the remaining 3 days can be worked remotely.</span></span></p><p style="margin:0px 0px 13.3333px;padding:0px;font-weight:normal;font-style:normal;background-color:transparent;text-align:left;"><span style="margin:0px;padding:0px;font-size:13px;line-height:18.6px;font-family:'Times New Roman', 'Times New Roman_EmbeddedFont', 'Times New Roman_MSCustomFont', 'Times New Roman_MSFontService', serif;"><span style="margin:0px;padding:0px;">We're a small, fast-moving French team backed by a German HQ. We need someone genuinely entrepreneurial who thrives on ownership rather than process, and who is both commercially sharp and technically curious – a strong communicator able to translate technical value