&lt;p&gt;As a Senior iOS Engineer, you’ll build new hospitality workflows and evolve established ordering experiences across iOS and Android. You’ll work with SwiftUI on the platform-specific UI and contribute to shared Kotlin Multiplatform business logic. The role involves complex mobile engineering across multi-device synchronisation, shared order state and a large, established application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join a small, experienced and fast-moving squad that works collaboratively through technical refinement, code reviews and pair programming. The team values engineers who communicate directly, challenge assumptions and proactively shape solutions rather than simply execute predefined tasks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and build new ordering experiences in SwiftUI, while evolving established capabilities such as table management, kitchen workflows and printer integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to shared Kotlin Multiplatform business logic and help shape the architecture of the ordering domain&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability and usability of ordering features used daily by hospitality merchants across phones, tablets and POS devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Android engineers and platform teams to maintain consistent cross-platform behaviour and reliable multi-device order synchronisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take part in code reviews, pair programming and collaborative testing to maintain a high quality bar&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help refine and scope upcoming work, bringing technical judgement to product and architectural trade-offs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to Mobile Chapter and KMP platform initiatives across the wider POS tribe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;You&#39;ll be great for this role if...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience building production iOS applications in Swift, with strong SwiftUI knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a large, established codebase and making pragmatic improvements without requiring a full rewrite&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Openness to learning and contributing to Kotlin and Kotlin Multiplatform; previous hands-on KMP experience is welcome but not required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work independently, challenge assumptions, propose solutions proactively and communicate clearly and directly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating closely with Android engineers or other cross-platform partners to align product behaviour&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Sound technical judgement and the ability to balance product delivery, code quality and long-term maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why you should join SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🌎 Opportunity to work with a truly global, multicultural team from our Paris location. This involves an office-first setup&lt;br&gt;🌈 Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion: be part of a workplace that values and promotes diversity, fostering an inclusive environment where everyone&#39;s perspectives are respected and embraced&lt;br&gt;🚀 Enrolment onto our Virtual Stock Option programme: you will own a stake in SumUp&#39;s future success&lt;br&gt;📚 A dedicated annual L&amp;amp;D budget of €2000 for your individual development, which can be used to attend conferences and/or advance your career through further education&lt;br&gt;💼 Financial security: corporate pension contributions that support your long-term future&lt;br&gt;🏥 Healthcare support: we cover 50% of the monthly cost of your health insurance for your Mutuelle and Prévoyance&lt;br&gt;🚌 Extra allowances: we offer restaurant tickets (Swile) and cover transportation costs&lt;br&gt;🌴 Break4me: 1-month sabbatical after 3 years of service&lt;br&gt;🔗 Referral Bonus: earn additional rewards by referring talented individuals to join the SumUp team&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About SumUp&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Be empowered to do more that matters.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At SumUp, we&#39;re on a mission to empower small businesses across the globe by providing simple and affordable tools that allow them to thrive. Today, over 4 million businesses in 39 markets rely on SumUp as their financial partner to manage payments, finance and customer relationships.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our commitment to small businesses is reflected in&lt;a href=&quot;https://youtu.be/9DG64C3moeQ?si=YpcWuBNBTOQPzeLI&quot;&gt; our diverse team&lt;/a&gt; of over 4,000 SumUppers from over 90 nationalities, united by global collaboration and an innovative mindset.&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/culture/&quot;&gt; Our core values&lt;/a&gt; lay the foundation for who we are and what we stand for, shaping our work culture and driving our success. We foster inclusivity and a continuous learning culture, providing a safe space for personal and professional growth. Our differences make us unique and strong as we strive to create an environment where everyone belongs and feels supported, no matter how they identify.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;SumUp is proud to be an Equal Employment Opportunity employer, actively seeking and embracing diversity in our workforce. We don&#39;t make hiring or employment decisions based on race, colour, religion or religious belief, ethnic or national origin, nationality, sex, gender, gender identity, sexual orientation, disability, age or any other basis protected by applicable laws or prohibited by company policy. Our commitment extends beyond recruitment to creating a safe and respectful workplace where harassment of any form is strictly prohibited. Discover more about our culture and opportunities on our&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sumup.com/careers/&quot;&gt; careers website&lt;/a&gt;, and follow our journey on&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.linkedin.com/company/sumup/&quot;&gt; LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;,&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.instagram.com/insidesumup/&quot;&gt; Instagram&lt;/a&gt;, and&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.tiktok.com/@insidesumup&quot;&gt; TikTok&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Job Application Tip&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;We recognise that candidates feel they need to meet 100% of the job criteria in order to apply for a job. Please note that this is only a guide. If you don’t tick every box, it’s ok too because it means you have room to learn and develop your career at SumUp.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/sumup/senior-ios-engineer-kmp-pos-paris-paris-283595","tags":["iOS"],"job_types":[],"location":"Paris, Paris","created_at":1791078904},{"slug":"business-development-representative-marche-francais-lyon-379550","company_name":"Amenitiz","title":"Business Development Representative - Marché Français","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>À propos du poste</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">En tant que <strong>Business Development Representative </strong>chez Amenitiz, vous prenez en charge l'intégralité du cycle de vente, du premier contact de prospection jusqu'à la signature du contrat. Il ne s'agit pas d'un poste centré uniquement sur la prise de rendez-vous. Vous prospectez, réalisez des démonstrations, traitez les objections et concluez les ventes, tout en gérant votre pipeline et votre contribution au chiffre d'affaires de bout en bout.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Nos clients sont des hôteliers indépendants partout en Europe : des établissements familiaux, des hôtels-boutiques et de petites chaînes hôtelières insuffisamment servis par des solutions technologiques conçues pour les grands groupes. Avec plus de 15 000 clients et une note de satisfaction de 4,8/5, notre produit bénéficie d'une forte reconnaissance sur le marché.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vous commercialiserez une solution qui a un impact concret et mesurable sur le quotidien de ses utilisateurs, tout en étant pleinement responsable de l'ensemble du processus qui leur permet d'y accéder.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>(Ce rôle est basé à Lyon, en France)</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Votre mission</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prospection et génération de pipeline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identifiez et contactez de nouveaux clients potentiels par téléphone, e-mail et chat. Maintenez un niveau d'activité élevé et construisez un pipeline commercial solide à partir de zéro. Vous êtes responsable de l'ensemble de votre activité de prospection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Découverte des besoins et qualification</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprenez l'organisation actuelle de chaque prospect, ses problématiques et ses besoins opérationnels. Identifiez rapidement les opportunités pertinentes et positionnez Amenitiz de manière précise et adaptée à leur situation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Démonstrations produit</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Animez des démonstrations structurées et personnalisées qui établissent un lien direct entre les fonctionnalités du produit et les enjeux métier du prospect. Rendez la prise de décision simple et évidente.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gestion des objections et closing</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Traitez avec assurance les hésitations, les comparaisons avec la concurrence et les objections liées au timing. Créez un sentiment d'urgence lorsque cela est pertinent et sachez demander la signature.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gestion du pipeline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintenez HubSpot à jour et garantissez la fiabilité des données. Réalisez des prévisions précises et assurez un suivi rigoureux de chaque opportunité.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaboration</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travaillez en étroite collaboration avec les responsables commerciaux et vos collègues afin d'améliorer en continu votre approche. Partagez les retours du marché, les objections récurrentes et les informations concurrentielles pour contribuer à la performance collective.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>À propos de vous</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vous disposez de 2 à 4 ans d'expérience dans une fonction commerciale (SDR, Account Executive ou poste en cycle de vente complet).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vous êtes de langue maternelle française, italienne, espagnole ou portugaise, et possédez un excellent niveau d'anglais, à l'écrit comme à l'oral.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vous êtes à l'aise pour alterner entre des phases de prospection intensive et des phases de closing au cours d'une même semaine.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vous assumez l'entière responsabilité de votre pipeline et de vos résultats, au-delà des simples indicateurs d'activité.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vous adoptez une approche structurée de la gestion commerciale : vos prévisions sont fiables et votre suivi est irréprochable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Vous faites preuve de résilience et de régularité dans un environnement exigeant, orienté objectifs et à fort volume d'activité.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Une expérience en SaaS, dans la technologie appliquée à l'hôtellerie ou en startup constitue un atout.<br />La maîtrise de HubSpot ou d'un CRM similaire est appréciée.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Ce que nous offrons</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Une rémunération attractive (OTE) composée d'un salaire fixe et de commissions déplafonnées basées sur la performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Des stock-options avec un calendrier d'acquisition progressif.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Une couverture santé complète.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Un accès anticipé à votre salaire, sans attendre la fin du mois.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Un parcours de carrière structuré, avec des critères d'évolution clairement définis à chaque niveau.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Des avantages flexibles permettant d'optimiser vos dépenses liées aux repas, à la garde d'enfants, aux transports et à la formation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">L'achat de tout livre professionnel dont vous avez besoin, ainsi qu'un accès à une bibliothèque partagée au sein de l'équipe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Une équipe internationale composée de plus de 35 nationalités, basée dans l'un des principaux hubs technologiques européens.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">#LI-LD1</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/amenitiz/business-development-representative-marche-francais-lyon-379550","tags":["Sales"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Lyon","created_at":1791078011},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-paris-346059","company_name":"Hcompany","title":"Senior Software Engineer - Paris","description":"<h2><strong>About H:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">When we released <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://hcompany.ai/newsroom/holo4">Holo4</a> on 28 September, we published every trajectory behind its public benchmark scores at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://trajectories.hcompany.ai">trajectories.hcompany.ai</a>. For OSWorld that's 369 desktop tasks, each run 3 times, with the steps, tokens and time of every attempt. This role builds and runs the evaluation framework that produces runs like these.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">H builds computer-use agents and the models behind them. Developers use them through a <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://hcompany.ai/newsroom/computer-use-agents-api">managed API</a>, and our forward deployed engineers take them into enterprise workflows.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>What this team owns</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The evaluation framework: orchestration, runtimes and observability. Researchers and forward deployed engineers bring the benchmarks, across web apps, desktop applications and the command line. Your job is to make the framework that runs them reliable, fast and cheap, and to make adding a new one quick. Research uses the results to choose checkpoints and decide whether a model ships. Product and the forward deployed engineers use them to measure agents on customer workflows. It carries roughly 50 benchmarks now. That number should be between 100 and 200 soon, and the framework has to keep up.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>What you'd be doing</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Integration support for researchers and forward deployed engineers bringing in a benchmark, with a shorter path each time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Setting the standard for how a benchmark enters the framework, and building the checks that enforce it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Scheduling and observability, so cluster capacity isn't left idle while evaluation jobs queue.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reproducible results across trials, so a release decision rests on numbers that hold.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Whatever stack a benchmark calls for. One week that's cluster tuning; the next it's a browser extension or desktop environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Time with customers, from single developers to large companies, to find out what they want measured, then automating it so the results flow back into our harnesses and models.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>The first few months</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">By 3 months you'll have helped researchers or forward deployed engineers integrate 5 benchmarks, and started fixing what slows the framework down. By 6 months one part of it is yours, for example scaling the runs, observability, or a group of related benchmarks, and a release will have gone out on your numbers. By 12 months you'll know the design and trade-offs of the whole evaluation system, and be the person the rest of H asks about evaluations.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>Who you'd work with</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ceiran Chapman, our VP Engineering, is hiring for this role. You'd join the evaluation team. The people relying on your work day to day are H's researchers and forward deployed engineers.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>What we think it takes</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Likely a good fit if you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have spent 5+ years in backend development, with production Python at the core, and use coding agents to go faster without letting quality drop.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built test, QA or evaluation tooling that other teams depended on, and care whether a number is right.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have operated distributed systems on Kubernetes in a public cloud. AWS experience helps most.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built and shipped systems end to end, including APIs (REST or GraphQL) and integrations with outside services.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Know relational and non-relational databases, and message queues such as SQS, RabbitMQ or Kafka.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instrument what you build, with metrics, tracing and monitoring from the start.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Stronger still if you have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Measured LLM quality before, or built agents yourself.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Packaged and run workloads in Docker and on virtual machines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Used Temporal, Dask, FastAPI, PostgreSQL, Grafana or Datadog.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automated web or desktop software with Playwright, Selenium or a browser extension you wrote.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set standards other engineers follow, through code review, design review or mentoring.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You do not need</strong> a background in machine learning. We'll work that out with you. If you match most of this but not all of it, apply anyway.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>How we hire</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">A 30 minute call with our Talent team, a 60 minute technical challenge, a 60 minute system design interview, and a 30 minute final conversation with Ceiran. About 3.5 hours in total.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h2>Practicalities</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Paris posting:</strong> Hybrid in Paris. That means 3 office days a week and a London trip about once every 4 to 6 weeks. There is a London posting for the same role. We offer a competitive package.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/hcompany/senior-software-engineer-paris-346059","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hybrid Paris","created_at":1791078010},{"slug":"automation-lead-villejuif-208586","company_name":"Orakl Oncology","title":"Automation Lead","description":"<h2><strong>About us, and our mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Orakl Oncology, we are accelerating the development of oncology treatments. Today, fewer than 5% of new cancer drugs succeed in clinical trials. Clearly, new methods are needed. We combine cutting-edge biology and AI to build the next generation of insight platforms with a large cohort of patient-derived tumor avatars. These avatars fuel our predictive engine, helping to anticipate clinical outcomes, validate therapies and uncover new drug candidates. By generating multimodal, real-world data, we aim to make drug development smarter, faster and more personalized. We collaborate with leading hospitals, research institutes and pharmaceutical companies. Backed by leading investors, Orakl is a fast-growing, mission-driven startup at the intersection of biology, automation and AI.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Position overview</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Orakl runs a high-throughput 3D cell‑culture platform to culture patient-derived organoids (PDOs). These patient-derived specimens reveal critical information into the patient disease, but require heavy maintenance work. Automating these workflows will be critical to improve the reliability and traceability of experimental work. We are hiring our first automation lead to build the Automation function from scratch. This is a high ownership and high autonomy job. You will map our processes, decide what to automate and what to leave alone, specify and source the equipment, negotiate with vendors and integrators, commission the machines, run them with the lab team, and hire the people the function needs. As the ideal candidate, you have already put automated lines or special machines into service, and you know what typically breaks between commissioning and the first experimental runs. While previous experience in biology is a plus, it is not a strict requirement: you will be taught all you need to know. However, you do need a proven experience in working deeply embedded in interdisciplinary teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key responsibilities</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Map cell culture workflows end to end and identify key process automation and optimisation opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the automation roadmap. Present and lead the implementation of the major decisions to Orakl’s leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In line with the automation strategy you will have identified, evaluate vendors and integrators. Write user requirement specifications, acceptance criteria and interface requirements for each project.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Negotiate price, scope, delivery, acceptance, support and consumables terms autonomously within agreed thresholds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead design reviews and factory and site acceptance tests.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate our proprietary cell culture protocols into automated machine execution with our team of cell biologists and scientists.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track machine availability, hands-on time per line, interventions, failures and recovery time. Use the data to decide the next step.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coordinate with Orakl’s management to anticipate future automation needs on the platform and adjust the roadmap accordingly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hire and develop the automation technicians and engineers the roadmap needs.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Set the standards for the automated platform: documentation, quality control, safety, qualification, change control, vendor management.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In this role you will collaborate closely with our cell culture, cell biology and data science teams. You will be at the heart of Orakl Oncology’s capabilities roadmap and help generate unprecedented amounts of biological data to power scientific discovery in cancer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Key qualifications</strong></h2><h3><strong>Must-have</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Engineering degree (generalist, robotics, industrial, mechanical or process engineering) or equivalent, and at least eight years of experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional process thinking skills: you map flows, time operations, find bottlenecks and question the processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in supplier negotiation and budget ownership on your own projects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in PLC and robot programming concepts, scheduling software, instrument interfaces, basic scripting.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You enjoy and are comfortable spending time on the floor with operators. You have experience in communicating and operating with engineers, technicians and workers at the heart of production processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Autonomy: you tell your manager what you decided and why, not what you need decided.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluency in English is required.</p></li></ul><h3><strong>Nice-to-have</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have put automated lines, cells or special machines into service end to end: requirements, vendor selection, negotiation, integration, factory and site acceptance, ramp-up, budget. This doesn’t have to be in a lab environment : plant, food and fermentation, pharma or cosmetics are other examples of relevant experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automation in life-science or regulated environments: cell culture, biotech, food and fermentation, pharma, cleanroom or BSL-2 work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A working understanding of cell culture and what it demands: sterility, contamination risk, variability between samples, and steps governed by the biological pace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Liquid handling, plate-based workflows, incubators and imagers; laboratory scheduling software.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience hiring and leading an automation team.</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What we offer</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will be Orakl's first automation hire. You will have a unique degree of ownership and scope with a strong mandate to deliver.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Short decision lines and fast execution.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An interdisciplinary environment with a results-driven culture.</p></li></ul><h3></h3><h2><strong>Recruitment process</strong></h2><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introductory call with Talent / People — 20 minutes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interview with the Lab Director, hiring manager — 45 minutes, including a 15-minute live mini-case on a small lab process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical deep dive with the CTO and the Lab Director</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case study on a real part of our lab: a take-home capped at four hours, then a half day on site with presentation, challenge round, lab walk.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cross-functional interviews with the technicians who run the culture, Platform Operations, the Senior Laboratory Engineers and the Data team — 60 minutes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reference calls: a former manager, a vendor or integrator you negotiated with, and an operator who ran a line you delivered</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founder conversation — 45 minutes</p></li></ol><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/orakl-oncology/automation-lead-villejuif-208586","tags":["Platform"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Villejuif","created_at":1791078007},{"slug":"product-manager-intern-platform-paris-68428","company_name":"mirakllabs","title":"Product Manager Intern - Platform","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Mirakl:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
