in-height:1.5em">Founded in 2024, we have grown to 90 people, raised over $60M, and increased revenue 40× this year. We are now entering a new phase of international expansion, industrial scaling, fundraising, and product development.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Role &amp; Mission</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />You will be the operational backbone of Alta Ares' field demonstration team — ensuring that every client and partner demonstration runs flawlessly, from equipment preparation through to mission debrief.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />On the ground, you are the go-to support for pilots, operators, and engineers: handling logistics, setting up and dismantling demo sites, keeping the equipment fleet in condition, and solving problems on the fly. Your versatility and resourcefulness set you apart — you move seamlessly from a hardware check to a client interaction, from a flight case to a transport declaration, without losing pace or precision.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Demonstration Preparation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare and verify all equipment before each mission: drones, ground control stations, batteries, and tooling</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pack into flight cases and conduct pre-departure checks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep inventories accurate and up to date</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Checklists &amp; Continuous Improvement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the operational and equipment checklists — execute them on the day</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Update checklists after each mission based on field feedback</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Formalise and improve processes continuously</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Logistics &amp; Transport</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organise outbound shipments and equipment returns</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare all transport documentation and coordinate with carriers and the supply chain</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure material arrives on time and in compliance with applicable regulations, including for sensitive or dual-use equipment</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Field Deployment</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Install and strike the demonstration site</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Support pilots during flight operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve as the on-site point of contact for ground teams, host nation staff, and client representatives</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equipment Maintenance</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monitor the condition of the demonstration fleet and report anomalies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Carry out first-level maintenance interventions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep the hardware mission-ready at all times</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Administrative Support</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare authorisation requests and write mission reports</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage expense claims and travel bookings</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep tracking tools up to date: backlog, planning, and mission logs</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Candidate Profile</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Military background or defence sector experience strongly valued: logistics, field support, or operations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Understanding of the defence ecosystem required — genuine commitment to national and European sovereignty</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Versatile and resourceful: you move from a manual handling task to a client conversation without missing a beat</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Rigorous on equipment and procedures — with the instinct to formalise and improve what can be</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working independently and as part of a team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Available for frequent travel, including internationally and in degraded security environments, sometimes at short notice</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional English — mandatory</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>French driving licence (Permis B) — mandatory</strong>; heavy goods licence (Poids Lourd) appreciated</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good physical condition — outdoor work and load carrying are part of the role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in drone piloting or the UAS/C-UAS ecosystem is a plus</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience shipping sensitive equipment is a plus</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/alta-ares/field-operations-specialist-paris-425593","tags":["Customer"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1791056407},{"slug":"human-design-program-lead-paris-74225","company_name":"Kraken","title":"Human Design Program Lead (F/H/X)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Help us use technology to make a big green dent in the universe!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://kraken.tech/"><u>Kraken</u></a> powers some of the most innovative global developments in energy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We create the technology that redefines utilities and unlocks a new energy system of the future. By optimising renewable generation, building a more intelligent grid, and empowering utilities to deliver an exceptional customer experience, our operating system is transforming the industry worldwide.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s an incredibly exciting time to work in energy. Join us on our mission to improve the lives of ONE BILLION humans within the decade and shape a cleaner, better future for everyone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">What we do: build the most AI-driven, innovative, forward-thinking platform for energy management. From optimizing resources to delivering cost-effective, exceptional customer experiences through advanced Customer Information Systems (CIS), billing, meter data management, CRM, and AI-driven communications, Kraken is powering the next wave of innovation in the energy industry.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">Why we do it: future energy will not look like energy as we know it today. We need to not just think about our future, but build for it. Now.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><h3><strong>🏡 Where you'll fit in:</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Kraken is the operating system of the future for Utilities. When a utility signs up to use Kraken, they have some big ambitions. They want to; improve customer experience, reduce cost to serve or accelerate growth and innovation. To make this possible at pace, clients need the incredible tech stack that Kraken offers, the ability to improve how they operate and to have a culture that enables them to thrive. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clients are increasingly interested in understanding how they can improve not only their customer operations but the business functions, and business units that sit horizontally and vertically to customer operations in retail. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To enable this Kraken now structures itself across 3 key delivery practice groups. Human Design, Org Design and Tech. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role sits within the Human Design Team. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Purpose of the Human Design Lead</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The main purpose of the Human Design Lead is to be the single point of accountability for the successful enablement and implementation of culture / ways of working transformation in our clients. Human Design activities align to Global Practices and include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Human enablement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behavioural transformation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership Development Programs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Coaching</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🚀 What you’ll own:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>New and existing senior clients’ relationships</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Actively involved in the end to end cycle of new clients’ pursuits, sales and onboarding</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Responsible for regional client portfolio (expected approx 4 clients)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Point of contact for senior client relationships long term</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">C-suite leadership coaching and enablement </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kick-start Human Design discussion with clients</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initial sprint setup including leading activities such as</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Line of Sight</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Culture survey</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exec LDP</p></li></ol></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Liaise with Human Design Global Practice Leads to influence and bring best practice into programs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead top-down cultural transformation, working with the C-suite and exec layer in organisations</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Senior cover for Human Design activities throughout migration including ongoing risk monitoring and escalation</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cultural stewardship</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Embody the Kraken ways of working and support the delivery team to do the same (and ensure a consistent experience across the portfolio)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as the bridge between new clients and best practice success stories</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>🧠 What you bring to the party:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In depth knowledge and expertise in all facets of Human Design necessary to enable transformation (including cultural transformation, leadership development, coaching, learning) </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in leading portfolios of major program transformations across different geographies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of trust-based partnerships with C-suite and executives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication skills at storytelling level across different seniorities and cultures</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent facilitation skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in navigating ambiguity and complexity </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear understanding of the connection between human, organisation and technology in the context of tech-enabled transformations </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience of working within the Energy, Utilities and Telco industries is highly desirable </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In depth knowledge of leadership and organisation behavioral best practices including concepts such as </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Psychological safety</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Empowerment </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth mindset </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Agile leadership </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High performing team</p></li></ul></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">What we’re looking for</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A systems thinker who is human-led based in <strong>Paris, France </strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a kind, friendly, human organisation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of adult learning, behaviour change and organisational psychology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A world-class and experienced leadership development expert.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A storyteller who deeply understands the art of facilitation </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven credibility working with senior leaders and executives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or scaling leadership or learning practices in complex environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Calm, confident and playful presence - able to challenge with empathy and clarity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fluent English &amp; French is a prerequisite </strong></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">As we are an English-speaking company, please provide your CV in English.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Kraken is a certified Great Place to Work in France, Germany, Spain, 