ty, take ownership, and keep going when things get hard. You're deeply curious, driven to understand how things work and how they can be improved. Most importantly, you have a strong bias to execution: you don't wait for perfect conditions, you ship, learn, and iterate quickly. If you care about building, moving fast, and making real impact, you'll fit right in.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What you'll do</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage and automate the fleet – build services for provisioning, health checks, upgrades, and incident remediation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Uphold reliability – embed observability, graceful degradation, and rollback paths into every layer you touch</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Architect the network – design and evolve a high-throughput, low-latency fabric tailored to our high performance use-cases</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ship software, not scripts – develop clean, testable code (mostly Go) that treats our fleet like a first-class API</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive efficiency – improve utilization and power-to-performance ratios so capacity grows slower than usage</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner across the stack – work with product, infra, and platform teams to scope and deliver features like storage-aware scheduling, cache volumes, and other developer-facing features</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h3><strong>What we're looking for</strong></h3><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience engineering large-scale infrastructure - writing the software that runs fleets, not just operating existing hyperscalers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depth in network architecture, data-center design, and performance tuning</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on time deploying and managing compute hardware at scale (servers, switches, etc)</p></li><l