rengths, and long-term goals.</p><h3><strong>What You’ll Be Doing (The Role) </strong></h3><p>As a Customer Experience Specialist, you will be the voice and face of global brands for <strong>German-speaking customers</strong> across Europe:</p><ul><li><strong>Be the Problem Solver:</strong> Assist customers via phone, live chat, and/or email with inquiries regarding products, order tracking, bookings, or account support.</li><li><strong>Deliver Top-Class Service:</strong> Turn tricky situations into positive customer moments through clear, empathetic, and friendly communication.</li><li><strong>Troubleshoot &amp; Guide:</strong> Walk users through basic technical issues, service setups, or account features step-by-step.</li><li><strong>Collaborate Globally:</strong> Work side-by-side with international colleagues in an inspiring, multicultural environment.</li><li><strong>Continuous Learning:</strong> Stay updated on the latest brand features, tools, and updates with ongoing support.</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li><strong>Fluency in German:</strong> Native or fluent (C1/C2 level) in both written and spoken communication.</li><li><strong>Good English Knowledge:</strong> (B2 level or higher) to navigate company systems and communicate with international team members.</li><li><strong>Work Eligibility:</strong> EU Passport or a valid legal work permit for Greece.</li><li><strong>Age Requirement:</strong> At least 18 years old.</li><li><strong>Digital Literacy:</strong> Comfortable navigating computers, multi-screen environments, and basic software applications.</li><li><strong>Soft Skills:</strong> Strong communication skills, active listening, empathy, and a positive problem-solving mindset.</li><li><strong>Relocation Readiness:</strong> Willingness and motivation to relocate to Greece in the coming weeks.</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><ul><li><strong>14 Salaries per Year:</strong> In Greece, you receive extra salary bonuses for Easter,