el that lets machines reason about the physical world and do work robots couldn't do before - starting with logistics.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a team of engineers and researchers with roots at ETH Zürich, backed by leading European investors. The technology is ambitious; now we want the way we look and show up to match it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You make Flink look as cool from the outside as it is on the inside. As our first brand &amp; marketing hire, you own how Flink shows up to the world and help shape how it feels to work here.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role with a lot of ownership from day one. You'll work directly with the CEO and the whole team, and you'll have real freedom to set the tone. We care more about taste, energy and drive than years of experience; junior profiles are very welcome.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll do</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Own our look and feel.</strong> Evolve and guard Flink's visual identity. Logo use, colours, typography, photo and video style: and make sure everything we put out is consistent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run our website.</strong> Keep<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://flink.so/"> </a><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://flink.so"><u>flink.so</u></a> fresh, fast and on-message: new pages, news, job posts, visuals. Work with freelancers or agencies where needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build our social presence.</strong> Plan and create content for LinkedIn and other channels. Robot footage, behind-the-scenes, team stories, milestones and grow an audience that gets excited about what we do.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run marketing campaigns.</strong> Turn our story into campaigns, from product launches and trade fair pushes to customer and recruiting campaigns. You own the creative and the message, and work closely with the Growth team on goals, audiences and channels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Tell our story visually.</strong> Create or coordinate photos, videos, graphics and animations of our robots and technology. Support pitch decks, investor updates and sales materials so they look world-class.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Organise events.</strong> From trade fairs and demo days to meetups, customer visits and team events. Plan them, run them and make them memorable.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Make our space amazing.</strong> Shape how our office and workshop look and feel, so every visitor - investor, customer or candidate - gets the Flink vibe.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strengthen our employer brand.</strong> Help us attract top engineers: careers page, job ads, recruiting content, how candidates experience Flink.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bring the brand inside.</strong> Help build team culture through internal communication, onboarding touches, swag; you name it.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A strong eye for design and visuals: you know what looks great.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Creativity and ideas of your own: you don't wait for a brief to start making things</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on skills in design tools (e.g. Figma, Adobe Creative Suite, Canva) and comfort creating content for social media</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A portfolio that shows your taste: professional, freelance, student or side projects all count</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Organisational talent: you can juggle an event, a website update and a video shoot in the same week</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent written and spoken English</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Curiosity about technology and robotics: you don't need to be an engineer, but you want to understand what we build</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">First experience in branding, marketing, design or communications (internships count)</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Nice to have</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">German (spoken or written)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Photo or video shooting and editing skills</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with website design</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Interior design, set design or event production experience</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Previous startup or tech-company experience</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The chance to build a brand from the ground up at a deep tech startup on the rise</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real ownership and direct access to the founders: your work is visible from day one</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Robots, a workshop and a story worth telling: some of the most exciting content in tech, waiting to be shown to the world</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A growing, ambitious team in Zürich</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary and employee stock options</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Budget and freedom to try new ideas</p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/flink/brand-manager-zurich-196111","tags":["Sales & Operations"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zürich","created_at":1791006011},{"slug":"chief-of-staff-zurich-124295","company_name":"Jua","title":"Chief of Staff","description":"<h2><strong>Overview</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Physical AI, a real model of the world, is the next trillion dollar opportunity and a foundational pillar for energy, robotics and superintelligence.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Jua we are building it now. Our models already run on four continents and help power the energy buildout needed to support ever larger intelligence.  </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are assembling a world-class team of researchers and entrepreneurial minds to turn this model into reality at global scale. If you want the opportunity of your life, come build physical AI with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>The Role</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work directly with Jua’s Leadership. You operate as a force multiplier — plugging into whatever's highest-leverage that day, from fundraising and investor work to product calls, deals, and fixing what's broken before it slows us down. What you're pulled into will shift as the business does — some stretches this is heavily fundraising and investor-facing, others it's operational firefighting or unsticking a cross-functional project. The pace is high, the context load is real, and you'll see everything. This is also a launchpad into an executive leadership role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is best suited for someone who has been an early-stage operator or ex-founder, and has hands-on experience with start-ups that are still in the build-phase. If that's you, expect a founder's vantage point on how Jua scales — the pace and stakes of building it yourself, without carrying it alone.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>What You Will Do</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Problem-solve directly with the leadership team on the highest-leverage issues across the business — from product, marketing and operations to fundraising and partnerships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sit in high-stakes meetings with customers, investors, and strategic partners, and turn what happens there into clear next steps.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring clarity to priorities and make sure decisions actually turn into action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build lightweight dashboards and operating rhythms that help the team learn from data that's still evolving — without pretending it's cleaner than it is.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the glue across the business: spot where cross-functional work is stuck and personally unblock it — including outside your core areas, whether that's a marketing crunch, a vendor issue, or whatever's fallen through the cracks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write sharp briefs, investor materials, and internal notes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Handle practical execution when it matters — travel, schedules, logistics, on-site coordination.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h1><strong>Who You Are</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fast learner who can switch contexts without dropping quality — the mix of what you're doing will genuinely change over time, and you're energised by that rather than needing it to settle.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Real depth in one or two areas, not experience scattered thinly across many — we'd rather see two or three things you've actually driven than a long list of things you've touched.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with data and analytical tools (vibe coding is enough) — precise enough to help the team make calls on metrics that are still taking shape, without waiting for perfect numbers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear, concise communicator who compresses complexity.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">High ownership and bias toward action.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with ambiguity — figuring things out as you go — and good at building real relationships across the team to