<p>You are our first quality hire. There is no dedicated quality team, no lab, and no playbook; you will design the test / fixture / process and then go build it.&nbsp;</p>
</div><br><strong>What you will do</strong><br><div>

<li>Define what hardware quality means for Gravis from ground up</li>
<li>Design and implement testing systems, jigs and fixtures from incoming inspection to product shipping</li>
<li>Document failures, root causes and mitigations, build a failure database and review regularly with design and production</li>
<li>Teardown and analysis of field returns, drive corrective actions</li>
<li>Own supplier quality: first article inspection, qualification, audits, and 8D follow-through</li>
<li>Tighten drawings and specifications; critical characteristics, unambiguous acceptance criteria</li>
<li>Help building our long-term reliability and environmental test strategy as we scale</li>

</div><br><strong>What we're looking for </strong><br><div>

<li>A university degree in mechanical, electrical, quality Engineering or equivalent practical experience</li>
<li>3+ years experience in quality / manufacturing engineering in low volume manufacturing</li>
<li>Hands on failure analysis and teardowns</li>
<li>CAD knowledge for designing fixtures</li>
<li>Experience in hand metrology</li>
<li>Solid understanding of mechanical and electrical systems</li>
<li>Good command of English, both written and spoken</li>

</div><br><strong>Beneficial skills </strong><br><div>

<li>Experience in GD&amp;T</li>
<li>Experience in SQL / python</li>
<li>Exposure to environmental / accelerated lifetime testing (e.g. vibration, shock, ingress, UV)</li>
<li>Fluency in Mandarin</li>
<li>Off-highway, agricultural, mining or other harsh-environment equipment&nbsp;</li>

</div><div>
<p>This is an opportunity to join a dynamic, multidisciplinary team and to be part of a company that is reshaping heavy construction.</p>
